AgentGuard
Built for DevFest Pakistan 2026.

Design ideas and credit
-----------------------
Several design decisions in the scanner were learned from reading the public documentation and source layout of the
Obscura project (https://github.com/h4ckf0r0day/obscura, Apache License 2.0):

  - one deny-set of network ranges shared by the literal-address check and the DNS-resolution check;
  - hardening a tool server (loopback by default, a token of at least 32 bytes for anything else, an Origin allow-list,
    bounds on request size);
  - a non-root container for a process that reads untrusted input;
  - CI hygiene (actions pinned to full commit hashes, minimal permissions, concurrency and timeouts);
  - accepted findings that must carry a written reason;
  - an AGENTS.md and a SKILL.md for AI agents;
  - fixtures that come in bad and good pairs, and keeping hidden page content away from the model.

No Obscura source code is included in this project. The implementations here were written from scratch in Python and
TypeScript. We did not adopt its stealth / anti-detection features.

